air pollution energy and security and  global warming  fixing these huge problems may seem  impossible but we don't need a miracle  we can save our Earth and clean our air  and we can start right now using the  technology we already have  I'm Mark Jacobson a professor of civil  and environmental engineering at  Stanford University  in this course I'll take you inside my  classroom and share the science and  strategies for building clean renewable  energy and storage for everything  from our transportation system and  electricity infrastructure to our  Industries and businesses  you will learn about the key  Technologies for harnessing the power of  the wind the water and the sun with  storage to meet all our energy needs you  will also learn how to make Power grids  efficient resilient and dependable  anywhere in the world and how to develop  and Implement a road map to transition  your country State Community or business  to 100 clean renewable energy  you don't have to be a scientist or an  engineer  these lessons are for anyone who wants  to understand the latest research about  what works what doesn't and why we'll  explain everything from photovoltaics to  hydroelectricity to wind turbines to  batteries to electrolyzers to heat pumps  and show you why renewable electricity  generation and storage won't just save  our planet  it'll also create new job opportunities  and energy to manufacture whether you  work in business government education or  the nonprofit sector this foundational  course will give you the Practical  knowledge you need to communicate about  those important issues with confidence  transform your organization and  contribute to a healthier planet
 

